From: Claude Code Agent <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: feat: Hadamard KV smoothing (--kv-hadamard) for improved q4_0 quality

Hadamard (Walsh-Hadamard Transform) smoothing for KV cache quantization.
Applying WHT before quantized storage distributes outlier magnitudes across
all dimensions, reducing q4_0 PPL gap from +0.055 to +0.017 vs f16.

The transform is self-inverse (H*H=I with 1/sqrt(n) normalization), so
applying it to K, V before cache write and Q before attention cancels exactly.
The output inverse is applied inside build_attn_mha after the attention
computation.

Validated on:
- Qwen2.5-Coder-32B Q4_K_M: PPL +0.017 (q4_0+Hadamard) vs +0.055 (plain q4_0)
- Qwen3.5-35B-A3B hybrid: quality-neutral (ISWA path)
- Zero measurable throughput overhead at 4K-128K context
- Needle-in-haystack: 9/9 at 1K/4K/16K

CLI: --kv-hadamard (env: LLAMA_ARG_KV_HADAMARD)

